      "initial_prompt": "ROUND 1 ONLY — SHARP CYCLIC POINCARE INEQUALITY VIA DFT.\n\nConsider an integer N >= 3 and a real sequence x_0,...,x_{N-1}, with x_N = x_0 and sum_{j=0}^{N-1} x_j = 0. Define E(x) = sum_j (x_{j+1}-x_j)^2 and M(x) = sum_j x_j^2.\n\nObjective: Prove rigorously that E(x) >= 4 sin^2(pi/N) M(x), establish optimality, and show that equality holds exactly for x_j = A cos(2 pi j/N) + B sin(2 pi j/N), where A,B are real. Prove that these two real vectors are linearly independent for every N >= 3, including N = 3.\n\nRequired proof: State a precise DFT convention and inverse transformation; establish Parseval's identity with the correct normalization; compute the discrete difference multiplier and its squared modulus; use the zero-mean hypothesis to eliminate the constant mode; compare all remaining eigenvalues rigorously; and identify exactly which frequencies achieve the minimum. Carefully address conjugate symmetry of Fourier coefficients for real sequences and the frequency identification modulo N. Demonstrate optimality by an explicit nonzero equality vector.\n\nBoundary audit: Treat N = 3 explicitly, including the fact that every mean-zero vector is an equality case. Treat N = 4 explicitly, identifying the two-dimensional equality space and the remaining mean-zero mode. Check the even-N Nyquist frequency and verify that no additional minimizing frequencies occur.\n\nDeliverable: A concise, self-contained mathematical report with status, summary, findings, proof evidence, obstacles, and recommended next steps, targeting approximately 700 words while retaining essential calculations. State clearly what has been proved rather than independently verified. Record the spectral values and orthogonality information needed for a subsequent deficit-to-distance stability theorem, but do not substitute that future task for the required Round 1 proof.\n\nThis is exactly one research round. Do not execute software, use external sources, propose unnecessary child creation, or proceed to Round 2. Stop after submitting the mandatory report to your parent coordinator."
